WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:03.536 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:03.536 --> 00:00:05.271
-In Surprise Inspection
this week,

00:00:05.271 --> 00:00:09.008
we did a lot of jokes
about the planet Uranus,

00:00:09.008 --> 00:00:10.242
and a bunch of you said

00:00:10.242 --> 00:00:13.379
that's not how that planet
is pronounced.

00:00:13.379 --> 00:00:16.082
If I had pronounced
it a different way,

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:19.152
my writers would have
gone on strike again.

00:00:23.122 --> 00:00:27.560
I opened the last episode saying
that I was not a boomer.

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.095
Bungee pointed out

00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:35.468
I still did a Jimmy Stewart
impression and made a Who joke.

00:00:35.468 --> 00:00:37.203
Very...

00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:41.808
What started as a kind comment,
I thought,

00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:44.376
about my
Jimmy Stewart impression,

00:00:44.376 --> 00:00:45.945
and then took a turn.

00:00:45.945 --> 00:00:52.051
"That Jimmy Stewart one
is out of this world.

00:00:52.051 --> 00:00:54.487
I can't recall a time
that I have heard one

00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:57.823
where absolutely none
of the basic elements

00:00:57.823 --> 00:01:01.194
of what makes his voice his
were used."

00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:04.831
[ Imitating Jimmy Stewart ]
"Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:06.766
Hey, there."

00:01:10.836 --> 00:01:12.638
Ooh, this one was bad.

00:01:12.638 --> 00:01:14.440
I guess, uh...

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:18.644
I did the Pete Townshend
windmill backwards.

00:01:18.644 --> 00:01:22.381
He famously did it like this
to end up.

00:01:22.381 --> 00:01:27.553
And I did it like this, but I
was told that was on purpose.

00:01:27.553 --> 00:01:32.092
NBC said we can't even afford
the residuals for the motion.

00:01:35.294 --> 00:01:37.497
I had to do a look-alike.

00:01:41.034 --> 00:01:42.969
Here's another nice comment.

00:01:42.969 --> 00:01:45.638
The last "Corrections"
was our 90th episode.

00:01:45.638 --> 00:01:49.876
"90 tries, no good jokes
or interesting stories.

00:01:49.876 --> 00:01:52.679
Let's see if something changes."

00:01:55.948 --> 00:01:59.885
Yeah, man. By all means,
stick it out.

00:01:59.885 --> 00:02:02.888
You obviously got a lot
going on.

00:02:02.888 --> 00:02:04.824
Well, obviously, on episode 90,

00:02:04.824 --> 00:02:06.759
we're not going to do a big
thing for the 100th episode.

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:08.094
A lot of people are asking.

00:02:08.094 --> 00:02:11.397
We did for the 50th episode.
We did a SpecJackular.

00:02:11.397 --> 00:02:14.566
And I stress that it was not
an episode of "Corrections."

00:02:14.566 --> 00:02:19.939
It was a special,
a pre-recorded variety special.

00:02:19.939 --> 00:02:23.710
And then we submitted it
in that category for the Emmys

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:26.712
and received a letter
from the Academy saying,

00:02:26.712 --> 00:02:30.516
"We don't consider this
a special,

00:02:30.516 --> 00:02:32.418
because it's not any different

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:35.154
from the other episodes
of 'Corrections.'"

00:02:35.154 --> 00:02:37.924
And to the Academy, I say, fair.

00:02:40.025 --> 00:02:41.861
Got us dead to rights
on that one.

00:02:41.861 --> 00:02:46.766
We tried to pull a fast one.
You caught us. Congratulations.

00:02:46.766 --> 00:02:49.302
Also, congratulations to
"I Think You Should Leave,"

00:02:49.302 --> 00:02:51.837
which did win
the Emmy for this category.

00:02:51.837 --> 00:02:54.507
Fantastic show by our friends
Tim and Zach.

00:02:54.507 --> 00:02:55.741
[ Light applause ]

00:02:55.741 --> 00:02:57.476
You know, you could also
applaud for "Corrections."

00:02:57.476 --> 00:02:59.445
[Bleep].

00:03:03.115 --> 00:03:04.317
Like, the whole time,

00:03:04.317 --> 00:03:07.020
I'm like, "Oh,
they just must never clap."

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:15.094
Biden said "a book of fiction."

00:03:15.094 --> 00:03:17.396
I called him out.
I said, "That's called a novel."

00:03:17.396 --> 00:03:18.598
A lot of you said,
a book of fiction

00:03:18.598 --> 00:03:20.866
could be a novella
or a book of poems.

00:03:20.866 --> 00:03:24.971
I personally,
I only read nonfiction poems.

00:03:24.971 --> 00:03:27.873
That's just me.
You might think it limits them.

00:03:27.873 --> 00:03:33.412
It doesn't. The nonfiction
limericks are worse.

00:03:33.412 --> 00:03:38.585
No one from Nantucket
has one that long.

00:03:42.288 --> 00:03:46.325
I said Alaskan Airlines.
It's Alaska Airlines.

00:03:46.325 --> 00:03:48.694
It used to be "Alaskan,"

00:03:48.694 --> 00:03:50.196
but then during a flight,

00:03:50.196 --> 00:03:52.298
the N just blew off.

00:03:56.436 --> 00:04:00.340
Just landed in a field
in Nashville,

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:02.308
which used to be Asheville.

00:04:09.215 --> 00:04:11.684
Someone said, "There are
very few pizza delivery men

00:04:11.684 --> 00:04:13.586
in porn anymore."

00:04:13.586 --> 00:04:15.320
That comment was sent in by...

00:04:15.320 --> 00:04:17.223
Anonymous.

00:04:20.993 --> 00:04:22.862
Had a joke about
peanut allergies

00:04:22.862 --> 00:04:24.163
in Surprise Inspection.

00:04:24.163 --> 00:04:26.498
Then we showed an insulin pen
instead of epi pen.

00:04:26.498 --> 00:04:28.501
We knew the joke
was about peanut allergies.

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:30.370
We just thought it was so bad,

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:33.106
it would give
the audience diabetes.

00:04:39.845 --> 00:04:42.248
Oh, I referenced the motorcycle
I was going to buy this weekend,

00:04:42.248 --> 00:04:44.049
and I said how excited I was

00:04:44.049 --> 00:04:46.519
to finally be able to go
"vroom vroom vroom."

00:04:46.519 --> 00:04:50.223
I guess you don't do both
at the same time,

00:04:50.223 --> 00:04:51.924
because only one
is the accelerator.

00:04:51.924 --> 00:04:53.659
I was told if I did this,

00:04:53.659 --> 00:04:56.095
"the bike would likely fly out
from under him,

00:04:56.095 --> 00:04:57.396
raking his legs as it went,

00:04:57.396 --> 00:05:00.733
pulling him along
like a ragdoll."

00:05:00.733 --> 00:05:05.304
I might pay to get both
be accelerators.

00:05:05.304 --> 00:05:09.575
I've got two-accelerator money.

00:05:09.575 --> 00:05:14.079
Oh, I was also told I don't
have to make the "vroom vroom."

00:05:14.079 --> 00:05:16.515
I guess that's included.

00:05:16.515 --> 00:05:18.551
Ooh.

00:05:18.551 --> 00:05:21.687
Talking a lot about pandas,
whether they eat meat or not.

00:05:21.687 --> 00:05:23.489
Um, pandas, here's a comment.

00:05:23.489 --> 00:05:24.857
Pandas are actually
"what's known as

00:05:24.857 --> 00:05:27.793
a facultative herbivore.

00:05:27.793 --> 00:05:31.897
They do better on a plant diet,
but can eat meat.

00:05:31.897 --> 00:05:35.334
There is a video of
a giant panda chasing, killing,

00:05:35.334 --> 00:05:37.102
and eating a peacock in a zoo."

00:05:37.102 --> 00:05:38.804
Now, obviously,
when I read that,

00:05:38.804 --> 00:05:40.172
I quickly went to YouTube,

00:05:40.172 --> 00:05:42.308
because I wanted to see
if that was true.

00:05:42.308 --> 00:05:44.477
It is true. I found the video.
We're going to show the video.

00:05:44.477 --> 00:05:46.712
I should warn you,
it's fairly graphic.

00:05:46.712 --> 00:05:48.113
It is what it says it is,

00:05:48.113 --> 00:05:50.649
so if that's not the kind
of thing you want to see,

00:05:50.649 --> 00:05:54.219
maybe skip this part
of a panda eating

00:05:54.219 --> 00:05:56.956
and killing a peacock at a zoo.

00:05:56.956 --> 00:05:58.658
Alex, do you want to show it?

00:05:58.991 --> 00:06:00.226
[ Peacock cawing ]

00:06:00.226 --> 00:06:02.194
[ Panda roaring ]

00:06:02.194 --> 00:06:05.664
[ Peacock cawing ]

00:06:05.664 --> 00:06:08.000 line:0%
♪♪

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:09.736
[ Splattering ]

00:06:23.716 --> 00:06:27.687
A court stenographer
doesn't use a typewriter.

00:06:27.687 --> 00:06:29.788
In my defense,
it is hard to remember

00:06:29.788 --> 00:06:32.024
the name of the machine
they use.

00:06:32.024 --> 00:06:33.658
A stenographer
doesn't use a typewriter.

00:06:33.658 --> 00:06:36.295
They use a stenograph.

00:06:36.295 --> 00:06:38.231
I should have said "stenograph,"

00:06:38.231 --> 00:06:39.498
or if I wanted
to keep "typewriter,"

00:06:39.498 --> 00:06:41.868
I should have said
the court typewriter-er.

00:06:46.071 --> 00:06:48.173
I said harakiri wrong.

00:06:48.173 --> 00:06:49.442
I hope I'm saying it right now.

00:06:49.442 --> 00:06:52.477
I said, "hare-kare."
I believe it's "hara-kiri."

00:06:52.477 --> 00:06:54.647
I have dishonored myself.

00:06:59.818 --> 00:07:01.821
If only there was a way...

00:07:07.426 --> 00:07:09.061
Someone wrote this.

00:07:09.061 --> 00:07:12.231
Someone, "Seth,
not exactly on topic,

00:07:12.231 --> 00:07:13.900
but I thought you should
know that your image,

00:07:13.900 --> 00:07:15.234
along with Kelly Clarkson's,

00:07:15.234 --> 00:07:17.970
is fraudulently being used
to sell a product

00:07:17.970 --> 00:07:20.472
called Pure Balanced Keto.

00:07:20.472 --> 00:07:22.074
I will attempt to send
a screenshot

00:07:22.074 --> 00:07:24.443
if I can find an appropriate
email address to send it to.

00:07:24.443 --> 00:07:26.412
Sue the bastards and keep up
the great work

00:07:26.412 --> 00:07:27.446
with 'Corrections.'
It's the best."

00:07:27.446 --> 00:07:29.815
Thank you
to whoever sent that in,

00:07:29.815 --> 00:07:33.652
and also thank you
to Pure Balanced Keto.

00:07:33.652 --> 00:07:37.023
Ever since I've started
taking it, I have more energy.

00:07:39.058 --> 00:07:41.026
I sleep better, I feel better.

00:07:41.026 --> 00:07:42.528
Isn't that right, Kelly?

00:07:42.528 --> 00:07:45.731
And then just, like,
cut her in, laughing,

00:07:45.731 --> 00:07:47.900
and then just
send me my [bleep] money.

00:07:52.504 --> 00:07:57.610
Showed an ornament of a...

00:07:57.610 --> 00:08:00.779
It was a Steeler
with the Mac Tonight head,

00:08:00.779 --> 00:08:02.314
and it said 12:37 on it.

00:08:02.314 --> 00:08:03.749
And I initially said, "Oh,

00:08:03.749 --> 00:08:05.451
somebody was trying to guess
the length of 'Corrections.'"

00:08:05.451 --> 00:08:07.686
And then somebody said, "No,
it's actually a Bible verse."

00:08:07.686 --> 00:08:08.787
And I looked up
the Bible verse,

00:08:08.787 --> 00:08:10.455
which is very apt to
"Corrections."

00:08:10.455 --> 00:08:12.291
And then last week
100 of you said,

00:08:12.291 --> 00:08:13.826
"No, you dip[bleep].

00:08:13.826 --> 00:08:15.928
It's what time
your show starts."

00:08:18.998 --> 00:08:21.366
That was definitely it.

00:08:21.366 --> 00:08:23.736
The last one I got to.

00:08:23.736 --> 00:08:27.773
Did a joke
about the kind of fake eye

00:08:27.773 --> 00:08:29.275
Ellen tried to get me to show.

00:08:29.275 --> 00:08:32.712
It was a bloody eye with
the nerves coming out of it,

00:08:32.712 --> 00:08:34.580
and I said, "Can you believe

00:08:34.580 --> 00:08:36.816
she wanted me
to show this on TV?

00:08:36.816 --> 00:08:38.050
The nerve."

00:08:38.050 --> 00:08:40.152
A lot of you said that was --

00:08:40.152 --> 00:08:41.753
I mean, that's
an A-plus joke, right?

00:08:41.753 --> 00:08:43.389
That's why you come
to "Corrections."

00:08:43.389 --> 00:08:47.460
And someone wrote,
"Bravo to whoever wrote that."

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:49.095
I wrote that joke.

00:08:51.930 --> 00:08:56.402
To quote Jo Koy, "I write
the ones you laugh at."

00:09:03.876 --> 00:09:07.613
That would have really
rang true for me.

00:09:07.613 --> 00:09:09.615
I turned 50 over the break.

00:09:09.615 --> 00:09:11.784
An interesting thing happens
right before you turn 50,

00:09:11.784 --> 00:09:13.452
for the weeks leading up to it,
people are like,

00:09:13.452 --> 00:09:15.454
"Oh, my God, are you excited?
You must be so excited.

00:09:15.454 --> 00:09:16.689
Where are you doing
on the big day?

00:09:16.689 --> 00:09:18.256
I can't wait to hear.
I hope it goes well."

00:09:18.256 --> 00:09:21.761
And then you turn 50 and no one
talks to you ever again.

00:09:21.761 --> 00:09:23.596
It's like you're invisible.

00:09:23.596 --> 00:09:27.532
It's like you're
a ghost, walking.

00:09:27.532 --> 00:09:28.967
I went to the automatic doors
of the grocery store.

00:09:28.967 --> 00:09:32.304
They didn't even open.

00:09:32.304 --> 00:09:36.509
[ Chuckles ] In that joke,
I go to the grocery store.

00:09:36.509 --> 00:09:38.610
Can you imagine?

00:09:38.610 --> 00:09:40.779
"Where's your milk," I guess.

00:09:40.779 --> 00:09:42.415
How do you say it?

00:09:45.918 --> 00:09:50.957
Hey, I did turn 50
and, you know,

00:09:50.957 --> 00:09:53.392
we got that P.O. box
that we set up,

00:09:53.392 --> 00:09:56.395
and received
some really lovely gifts.

00:09:56.395 --> 00:09:58.297
This is a fantastic.

00:09:58.297 --> 00:10:01.299
I got some
Animal Flubs finger puppets.

00:10:01.299 --> 00:10:02.834
Look at those. Beautiful.

00:10:02.834 --> 00:10:05.037
That's a really great gift.
Thank you so much.

00:10:05.037 --> 00:10:07.906
Also,
I will say we did a very long

00:10:07.906 --> 00:10:10.142
"Animal Flubs" song
the last "Corrections,"

00:10:10.142 --> 00:10:12.945
and I think a bunch of
you hit your breaking point

00:10:12.945 --> 00:10:14.780
and asked me
never to do it again.

00:10:14.780 --> 00:10:17.083
And so that is
a New Year's resolution

00:10:17.083 --> 00:10:20.152
is no more "Animal Flubs" songs.

00:10:20.152 --> 00:10:21.753
I want you to know,
I heard it loud and clear.

00:10:21.753 --> 00:10:23.522
I don't know
if this is really from OSHA,

00:10:23.522 --> 00:10:25.023
but have you ever heard of OSHA?

00:10:25.023 --> 00:10:27.159
That's the Occupational Safety
and Health Administration,

00:10:27.159 --> 00:10:28.427
and this is,

00:10:28.427 --> 00:10:31.263
"For your safety and
the safety of those around you."

00:10:31.263 --> 00:10:34.133
And it is a pencil
with a cork on it,

00:10:34.133 --> 00:10:36.168
because a lot of people --
we talked about

00:10:36.168 --> 00:10:37.502
how I'm almost going to
take my eye out,

00:10:37.502 --> 00:10:38.770
so I'll be using that
from now on.

00:10:38.770 --> 00:10:39.939
Thank you very much.

00:10:39.939 --> 00:10:42.941
We got our 3D printer friend

00:10:42.941 --> 00:10:46.312
and he made me, um --

00:10:46.312 --> 00:10:50.316
this, by the way,
you should really look away.

00:10:50.316 --> 00:10:55.187
The panda thing was a joke.
This is actually distressing.

00:10:55.187 --> 00:10:56.789
He said, "I sent you
a Meyer lemon."

00:10:59.124 --> 00:11:01.827
[ Audience groans ]

00:11:06.198 --> 00:11:09.601
It's very, uh, flattering...

00:11:09.601 --> 00:11:13.772
emphasis on "flat."

00:11:13.772 --> 00:11:16.041
Oh, and then,

00:11:16.041 --> 00:11:19.811
someone said there was a...

00:11:19.811 --> 00:11:22.581
Amber did something about
how she wanted her own Barbie.

00:11:22.581 --> 00:11:25.984
And someone
sent this in for Amber

00:11:25.984 --> 00:11:27.687
with the loveliest card.

00:11:27.687 --> 00:11:29.454
And, you know,
when I was looking at it,

00:11:29.454 --> 00:11:30.522
I couldn't help but think,

00:11:30.522 --> 00:11:33.759
"That's not what
my P.O. box is for."

00:11:36.295 --> 00:11:38.631
Okay?

00:11:38.631 --> 00:11:41.066
If Amber wants a P.O. box
to get gifts,

00:11:41.066 --> 00:11:42.367
she can set up her own P.O. box.

00:11:42.367 --> 00:11:44.470
It's not that hard.

00:11:44.470 --> 00:11:45.771
You just go to your assistant,
you go,

00:11:45.771 --> 00:11:47.606
[Whining] "Will you
set up a P.O. box?"

00:11:53.312 --> 00:11:55.414
Oh, and then,
this is really special.

00:11:55.414 --> 00:11:56.549
You guys know
I'm a Steelers fan.

00:11:56.549 --> 00:11:59.418
The camera crew got me
an autographed

00:11:59.418 --> 00:12:00.919
Lynn Swann jersey.

00:12:00.919 --> 00:12:02.053
Look at that.

00:12:02.053 --> 00:12:03.422
Here's the autograph,
it's on this side.

00:12:03.422 --> 00:12:04.656
Lynn Swann, if you don't know,

00:12:04.656 --> 00:12:06.358
was a wide receiver
from the Steelers

00:12:06.358 --> 00:12:09.128
who weighed 800 pounds.

00:12:13.098 --> 00:12:17.369
Just so graceful,
and they got my size, 5XL.

00:12:26.778 --> 00:12:28.113
I'm going to have --

00:12:28.113 --> 00:12:29.881
You know how many more years
I'm going to have to work

00:12:29.881 --> 00:12:32.852
to afford to frame this?

00:12:38.824 --> 00:12:44.295
This is like if David Byrne
was a wide receiver.

00:12:44.295 --> 00:12:47.866
I am a boomer. [ Laughs ]

00:12:47.866 --> 00:12:50.235
Oh, and chewing --

00:12:50.235 --> 00:12:52.003
We've been talking about
how I chew my fingernails,

00:12:52.003 --> 00:12:55.474
and that's another
New Year's resolution.

00:12:55.474 --> 00:12:58.377
I've tried to stop
chewing my fingers,

00:12:58.377 --> 00:12:59.978
and we'll keep an eye on it.

00:12:59.978 --> 00:13:02.148
Let's take a look
at how I'm doing.

00:13:03.715 --> 00:13:05.851
-♪ Animal flubs, animal flubs ♪

00:13:05.851 --> 00:13:08.587
♪ It's time to take a look
at some animal flubs ♪

00:13:08.587 --> 00:13:11.757
♪ From the birds to the bees
to the baby bear cubs ♪

00:13:11.757 --> 00:13:14.226
♪ It's time for animal flubs ♪

00:13:14.226 --> 00:13:17.462
-♪ And I know, you don't
need to say "baby" ♪

00:13:17.462 --> 00:13:20.399
♪ Before you say "bear cub" ♪

00:13:20.399 --> 00:13:25.704
♪ Because in that case,
"cub" means "baby" ♪

00:13:25.704 --> 00:13:28.773
♪ But when you're writing a song
on a Thursday afternoon ♪

00:13:28.773 --> 00:13:31.843
♪ When you really should be
working on "A Closer Look" ♪

00:13:31.843 --> 00:13:34.747
♪ Sometimes you're gonna cut
a few corners ♪

00:13:34.747 --> 00:13:37.982
♪ In order to make
the rhyme scheme work ♪

00:13:37.982 --> 00:13:40.385
-♪ Animal flubs, animal flubs ♪

00:13:40.385 --> 00:13:43.621
♪ I hope you're all ready
for some animal flubs ♪

00:13:43.621 --> 00:13:46.124
♪ Call all your pals,
bunnies and pups ♪

00:13:46.124 --> 00:13:48.460
♪ It's time for animal flubs ♪

00:13:48.460 --> 00:13:50.562
-F.
-L.

00:13:50.562 --> 00:13:52.597
-U.
-B.

00:13:52.597 --> 00:13:53.966
